$ (session 2) fix: build-release.sh now auto-syncs Release/latest.json zipSHA256/zipSize/dmgSHA256/dmgSize from the artifacts it just built, instead of requiring a hand edit. Root cause: DMG/ZIP output is not byte-reproducible run to run (embedded timestamps), so the old hand-edit workflow silently desynced on every rebuild — exactly what session 1 caught. Verified via:
$ bash Scripts/build-release.sh 0.7.0 && bash Scripts/test-release-manifest.sh
=> ALL CHECKS PASSED (SHA256SUMS verifies, latest.json zip/dmg SHA+size match SHA256SUMS and actual files).
Added regression check to Scripts/test-release-manifest.sh: runs build-release.sh again and confirms latest.json resyncs to the newly-rebuilt (differently-hashed) artifacts, so the drift class cannot silently return.
